 class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-19T09:39:24-08:00","id":1546132,"title":"","content":"Having listened to some of these now, I'm a bit confused how I'm meant to take them.<br /> <br /> They seem to be being delivered in-character (there's a lot of &quot;I've only seen it once, but I have seen it&quot; for stuff that happens in-universe) and some of it seems to either contradict or at least raise questions about what's in the actual books, which makes it less helpful than it could be.<br /> <br /> For example: there's a reference in the Primal video to a woman whose Wild Form was &quot;like a great griffin&quot;. Is that, like, actually a legitimate Wild Form? It's true that the only restriction cited in the book is &quot;larger than their human form&quot; but it seems weird that you need a specific spell to turn into a mundane animal but not to turn into a full-on heraldic beast. There's also the recurring question of what happens with wings in that case.<br /> <br /> The idea that Elder Primals also just straight up know how to cure Damnations is kind of a bombshell too. The description in the book strongly implies that they've been looking for that secret but never found it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-19T13:11:45-08:00","id":1546152,"title":"","content":"It's in character and these are official lore drops about the various Families. Yes, the eldest Raptors claim they can release worthy Accursed from their Damnations. And yes, the Wild Form is a hybrid form, it's not just a big wolf or cat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-19T14:32:40-08:00","id":1546156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544400-the-gentleman-s-guide-to-the-accursed-youtube-series?p=1546152#post1546152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's in character and these are official lore drops about the various Families. Yes, the eldest Raptors claim they can release worthy Accursed from their Damnations. And yes, the Wild Form is a hybrid form, it's not just a big wolf or cat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right but can it be a totally non- human hybrid? Like can a Raptor's Wild form be a straight up dragon?<br /> <br /> Conversely is a very large mundane animal a valid wild form? Can a Lykan's wild form be a Dire Wolf? (Like WoD Hispo).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-20T01:17:33-08:00","id":1546182,"title":"","content":"I imagine every Wild Form has a human aspect to it, but they don't <i>need </i>to appear humanoid. If you want your Wild Form to resemble a dire wolf, you absolutely can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-20T10:12:03-08:00","id":1546200,"title":"","content":"Having listened to most of these now, a lot of this is absolutely the kind of content I'm happy to see siloed into bonus content (I don't actually need to know the IC myths about Family Origins and some of them are in the book anyway) but some of this really needs to be in the book. In particular it's mentioned in multiple places that Outcasts don't age like regular humans, but the books don't seem to make that clear (and in a lot of places it's stated that Outcasts basically *are* regular humans, they're directly compared to Sorcerers in those terms).<br /> <br /> [Edit]<br /> <br /> Oh, and the other thing that struck me as really needing to be in the books. It's mentioned that Ascetics use some kind of keyword to make you literally tell them your secrets. If that's how Ascetic feeding is meant to work it really, really needs to be in the book. (Also that's a flavour text ability which absolutely replicates the effects of game mechanical abilities many of which are gated behind Entanglement, CD expenditure, or other limited resources).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28625,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","user":"Nobody Special","date":". 11-22-2024, 03:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-25T07:38:11-08:00","id":1546384,"title":"","content":"Yeah, this is definitely stuff I'd love to see in a Book of Family Lore supplement. As bonus content, it is awesome, though.<br /> <br /> I'm memorizing it all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-25T09:36:00-08:00","id":1546391,"title":"","content":"Aah, I'd been waiting for this one. <br /> <br /> I like that souls are kept ambiguous and that there's uncertainty about family origins (although that feels stranger when the origin is so recent).<br /> <br /> I do have some confusion about how this works in play. The implication here is very strongly that Vorare work Shang Tsung style: they can just suck your soul straight out of you in what seems like combat time. And it now being more or less cannon that this turns people into Drones means that this feels like quite a major supernatural power the Vorare get pretty much for free.<br /> <br /> Is that how it's actually intended to be run?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-25T09:44:37-08:00","id":1546393,"title":"","content":"Here are your <a href=\"https://youtu.be/4JcduDac_Dw\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Vorare </b></a>(now in much better video quality, for those who want to see my face moving without pixilation).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style