te:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-04T10:00:13-08:00","id":1546593,"title":"","content":"How does being adopted ivy the Chimerae work? They seem fundamentally physiologically different from other Outcasts. It almost seems like it would be easier for a regular human to become one than somebody who was already a particular type of supernatural being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-09T09:02:23-08:00","id":1546798,"title":"","content":"The Gentleman's Guide to the <a href=\"https://youtu.be/J-PXilx1k9I?si=fKOy1Zu7u9Y7F643\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Premiere</b></a>!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-16T09:06:14-08:00","id":1547061,"title":"","content":"The Gentleman's Guide to the <b>Shades </b>for you kind folx: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tFpa2Z9JrfI\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tFpa2Z9JrfI</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-23T09:38:27-08:00","id":1547202,"title":"","content":"It's the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fqM-pYVPag0\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Gaki</b></a>!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-24T04:26:43-08:00","id":1547216,"title":"","content":"How do you envisage things like the Gaki immortality racket playing out in game? Like game mechanically.<br /> <br /> As far as I can tell there's no indication that they have any ability to ensure that a person comes back as a ghost, or of ensuring that the resulting phantasm will be sentient. Is this another thing that's meant to be beyond the scope of Entanglement 1-4?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-24T06:37:33-08:00","id":1547219,"title":"","content":"They will hunt in places where phantasms are most common. Sites where deaths took place and places of great emotional resonance. And with their Family inheritance they can summon those ghosts very easily. A Gaki with their Hungry Path as Major will find it harder, but not impossible, as they only need to sense a phantasm (hearing one is as good as seeing) to feed from one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-02T04:13:03-08:00","id":1547452,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the clarifications. Once again these *really* need to be in the book (RAW nothing says Gaki can interact with Incorporeal beings).<br /> <br /> A quick note on the Inheritance. The way you're describing it (and the way you seem to have run it in <i>Suffer My Sins</i>) doesn't seem to be how it actually works. It spare to be an innate ability to summon a generic phantasm with a particular template wherever you are and its use is strictly limited. There's no indication in the rules that Gaki can summon a specific phantasm, or that they'd actually gain any benefit from being in a graveyard. As currently worded out feels like a video game summon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-06T09:07:04-08:00","id":1547591,"title":"","content":"The <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ckEgkHkBCrI\" target=\"_blank\"><b>League of the Hidden Crossroads</b></a> is here!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-06T12:49:01-08:00","id":1547603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544400-the-gentleman-s-guide-to-the-accursed-youtube-series?p=1545140#post1545140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah that's fair, I was asking mostly because I'm getting to work out how I feel about it myself. Like it bothers me in a way the Ordo Dracul didn't even though Dracula is *also* either strongly implied or outright stated to be Vlad the Impaler who is also a real and highly controversial historical figure.</div> </div> </div> </div> When it comes to Count Dracula\u2019s Drunk History Rant from the novel, I\u2019ve always assumed that he was the \u201cDracula of a later age\u201d rather than that vague/possibly coded reference to the historic Impaler (If only because Count Dracula as someone who admired the historic Dracula - and presumably his father, who originated the name - is a more flexible character than an Actual Historic Person turned vampire).<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, whenever I consider Lord Ruthven (THE VAMPYRE) in recent days, it amuses me to note that - despite very possibly being Patient Zero for the aristocratic vampire and absolutely getting away with his villainy scot-free at the end of his novella, he\u2019s never yet been been the subject of any significant adaptation or follow-up (While Count Dracula and Countess Karnstein, both confirmed destroyed at the end of their tales, seem to have been given a \u2018Get out of Hell free\u2019 card, with multiple generations hungry for further adventures or some new slant on their stories).<br /> <br /> In an odd sort of way this surprising obscurity makes him feel MORE dangerous than many of his descendants: one can easily imagine him going on with his low-key international and occasionally murderous villainy for the rest of time, making every deliberate effort (albeit with a lovingly-cultivated aura of effortlessness) to keep his name, demeanour and history out of the public eye, all the better to bleed the unwitting dry.<br /> <br /> Not something I can say of the literary CARMILLA (Who would seem to regard her own condition with some degree of ambivalence and who is almost certainly lonely) and DRACULA (Who is very definitely in the undead equivalent of a Midlife crisis, with at least some hints that he\u2019s grown bored and at least a little ashamed of his skulking, secretive, predatory existence).<br /> <br /> Anyway, I do love the mental image of Lord Ruthven being greeted with \u201cNever heard of you\u201d or \u201cI don\u2019t know you\u201d only to reply \u201cHow very useful\u201d and an expression that is not a smile.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-07T05:29:46-08:00","id":1547615,"title":"","content":"I think I was thinking more of WoD/CofD Dracula who is (ISTR) more explicitly *that* Dracula although possibly CofD keeps it more ambiguous, I don't remember off the top of my head. <br /> <br /> (Also I'm not sure it *really* makes sense for boom Dracula not to be *that* Dracula, as I understand it the -a suffix basically literally means &quot;son of&quot; and AFAIK there's only ever been one notable Dracul and one notable Dracula despite his having had a brother).<br /> <br /> Although thinking about it (and as I've said this is probably going to be my headcanon) it's pretty plausible that the head of the Bathorites isn't the real Bathory either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-13T09:03:08-08:00","id":1547712,"title":"","content":"Quick, <a href=\"https